{"id":"word:hebrew:H3847","type":"word","title":"לָבַשׁ","subtitle":"H3847 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, wrap around , i.e. (by implication) to put on a garment or clothe (oneself, or another), literally or figuratively","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to לָבַשׁ (H3847) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 111 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"לָבַשׁ (lâbash) means properly, wrap around , i.e. (by implication) to put on a garment or clothe (oneself, or another), literally or figuratively First listed occurrence: 1Chr 12 19."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"לָבַשׁ","transliteration":"lâbash","pronunciation":"law-bash'","strong":"H3847","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3847","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יַּלְבֵּ֤שׁ","מְלֻבָּשִׁ֤ים","לְבַ֣שׁ","יִלְבְּשׁ֣וּ","לְב֣וּשׁ"],"morphs":[["HVqi3mp",9],["HVqsmsa",6],["HC/Vhw3ms",6],["HC/Vqw3ms",5],["HVqi3ms",5],["HVqp3ms",5],["HVPsmpa",4],["HVqsmsc",4],["HC/Vhq2ms",4],["HC/Vqq3ms",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, wrap around , i.e. (by implication) to put on a garment or clothe (oneself, or another), literally or figuratively","usage":"(in) apparel, arm, array (self), clothe (self), come upon, put (on, upon), wear.","full":"H3847. labash or labesh לָבַשׁ לָבֵשׁ verb put on (a garment), wear, clothe, be clothed (Late Hebrew id. ; Aramaic לָבֵישׁ , Assyrian labâšu ; Arabic ; Ethiopic ); — Qal Perfect 3 masculine singular לָבֵשׁ Psa 93:1 (twice in verse), לָבַשׁ Job 7:5 2 t., וְלָבַשׁ (consecutive) Lev 6:3 3 t.; suffix וּלְבָשֵׁם (consecutive) 16:4 ; 3 feminine singular לָֽבְשָׁה Judg 6:34 2 t., etc. ( Ezek 42:14 read probably וְלָֽבְשׁוּ Qr, for ילבשׁו Kt, but clause perhaps interpolated, see Co); Imperfect 3masculine singular יִלְבַּשׁ Deut 22:5 +; suffix וַיִּלְבָּשֵׁנִי Job 29:14 יִלְבָּשָׁם Exod 29:30 ; 1 singular suffix אֶלְבָּשֶׁ֑נָּה Song 5:3 ; 3 feminine plural תִּלְבַּשְׁןָ 2Sam 13:18 , etc.; Imperative masculine singular לְבַשׁ 1Kin 22:30 , etc.; Infinitive absolute לָבוֺשׁ Hag 1:6 ; construct לִלְבּשׁ Gen 28:20 ; Lev 21:10 ; Participle active plural הַלֹּבְשִׁים Zeph 1:8 ; passive absolute לָבוּשׁ 1Sam 17:5 ; Dan 10:5 ; לָבֻשׁ Ezek 9:2-3 t.; construct לְבוּשׁ Dan 12:6-7 , לְבֻשׁ Ezek 9:11 3 t.; plural construct לְבֻשֵׁי 23:6 2 t.; — 1. a. literally put on (one's own) garment (accusative) Gen 38:19 ; 1Sam 28:8 ; 2Sam 14:2 ; 1Kin 22:30 2Chr 18:29 ; Exod 29:30 ; Lev 6:3 ; 6:4 ; 16:4 (twice in verse); 16:23-24 , 32 ; 21:10 ; Deut 22:5 ; Ezek 44:17 , 19 , and so 42:14 Qr (see above), Jonah 3:5 ; Song 5:3 ; Est 4:1 ; 5:1 ; with accusative garment + עַלבְּֿשָׂרוֺ Lev 16:3 ; of putting on armour Jer 46:4 ; = wear (more or less habitually), with accusative of garment, Isa 4:1 ; Deut 22:11 ; Zeph 1:8 ; Zech 13:4 ; of Jerusalem under figure of woman Jer 4:30 , of rulers under figure of shepherds Ezek 34:3 , compare תִּלְבַּשְׁןָ כֵּן 2Sam 13:18 (no accusative) b. very often figurative , put on, be clothed with , with accusative of garment; — רִמָּה בְּשָׂרִי לָבַשׁ Job 7:5 my flesh is clothed (i.e. covered) with worms ; of Jerusalem, be clothed with inhabitants Isa 49:18 ; of pasture, with flocks Psalm 65:14; more often the garment is some abstract quality, e.g. righteousness, majesty, beauty, strength, etc.; &#8212; כַּשִּׁרְיָן צְדָקָה וַיִּלְבַּשׁ 59:17 he ( ׳י ) hath put on righteousness as a breastplate , compare 59:17 (vengeance), Psa 93:1 (majesty), 93:1 (strength), 104:1 (honour and majesty), Isa 51:9 (strength); also Job 40:10 ; said of men, 2Chr 6:41 (salvation), Psa 132:9 (righteousness), Job 29:14 ( id. ); of Zion Isa 52:1 (twice in verse); also in bad sense, clothed with terror, trembling, shame, etc., Ezek 7:27 ; 26:16 ; Job 8:22 ; Psa 35:26 ; 109:29 , compare 35:18 (cursing). c. literally put on , object omitted, לִלְבּשׁ נָתַןבֶּ֗֗֗גֶד Gen 28:20 ; Job 27:17 ; Infinitive absolute לָבוֺשׁ Hag 1:6 (there is) a clothing , but he has nothing for warmth. d. once with בּוֺ לָבַשׁ לְבוּשׁאֲ֗֗֗שֶׁר בְּ Est 6:8 . e. Passive participle, clothed with , chiefly Ezek.; &#8212; with accusative of garment, Ezek 9:2-3 , Zech 3:3 ; Prov 31:21 ; Dan 10:5 ; of wearing armour 1Sam 17:5 ; construct before garment, הַבַּדִּים לְבֻשׁ Ezek 9:11 ; 10:2 , 6 , 7 , compare 23:6 , 12 ; 38:4 ; Dan 12:6-7 ,. f. figurative: — י ׳וְרוּחַ אֶתגִּֿדְע֑וֺן לָֽבְשָׁה Judg 6:34 and the spirit of ׳י clothed itself with Gideon , i.e. (GFM) took possession of him (compare possessed ); so 1Chr 12:18 ; 2Chr 24:20 ; וַיִּלְבָּשֵׁנִי לָבַשְׁתִּי צֶדֶק Job 29:14 and it clothed itself in me, as it were, became incarnate in me. Pu`al only Participle plural מְלֻבָּשִׁים arrayed , with accusative of garment 1Kin 22:10 2Chr 18:9 ; 5:12 ; absolute in full apparel Ezra 3:10 . Hiph`il Perfect 3masculine singular suffix הִלְבִּישַׁנִי Isa 61:10 ; 3 feminine singular הִלְבִּישָׁה Gen 27:16 ; 2 masculine singular וְהִלְבַּשְׁתָּ֫ Exod 28:41 3 t.; suffix וְהִלְבַּשְׁתָּם (consecutive) 29:8 ; Num 20:26 ; 1 singular suffix וְהִלְבַּשְׁתִּיו Isa 22:21 ; 3 plural הִלְבִּישׁוּ 2Chr 28:15 , וְהִלְבִּשׁוּ (consecutive) Est 6:9 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular וַיַּלְבֵּשׁ Gen 41:42 5 t.; suffix וַיַּלְבִּשֵׁם 3:21 ; Lev 8:13 ; 3 feminine singular תַּלְבִּישׁ Prov 23:21 , etc.; Infinitive absolute הַלְבֵּשׁ Zech 3:4 ; construct הַלְבִּישׁ Est 4:4 ; Participle suffix הַמַּלְבִּשְׁכֶם 1Sam 1:24 ; &#8212; clothe, array with . 1 usually with 2 accusative , a. literal בִּגְדֵישֵֿׁשׁ אֹתוֺ וַיּלְבֵּשׁ Gen 41:42 ; 2Sam 1:24 ; Isa 22:21 ; Exod 28:41 ; 29:5 , 8 ; 40:13-14 , Lev 8:7 , 13 ; Num 20:26 , 28 ; Zech 3:4-5 , of clothing Jerusalem under figure of infant Ezek 16:10 ; of putting armour on some one 1Sam 17:38 (twice in verse). b. figurative , Job 10:11 thou hast clothed me with skin and flesh ; compare 39:19 (quivering of horse's neck); Isa 50:3 ; 61:10 ; Psa 132:16 ; 132:18 . 2 with accusative garment only , Gen 27:16 ( + עַליָֿדָיו ); figurative, Prov 23:21 . 3 with accusative of person only , Gen 3:21 ; 27:15 ; 2Chr 28:15 (twice in verse); Est 4:4 ; 6:9 , 11 . [ לְבֵשׁ ] verb be clothed (see Biblical Hebrew); — Pe`al Imperfect accusative אַרְנְּוָנָא : 3 masculine singular יִלְבַּשׁ . Dan 5:7 , 2 masculine singular תִּלְבַּשׁ 5:16 . Haph`el Perfect 3masculine plural הַלְבִּ֫שׁוּ Dan 5:29 clothe one ( ל ) with (accusative).","rootNote":"or לָבֵשׁ ; a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 12 19","keyReferences":["1Chr 12 19","1Kgs 22 10","1Kgs 22 30","1Sam 17 5","1Sam 17 38","1Sam 17 38","1Sam 28 8","2Chr 5 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":111,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 12 19","book":"1Chr","chapter":12,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָבְשָׁ֗ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3fs"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 10","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְלֻבָּשִׁ֤ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVPsmpa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 30","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְבַ֣שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqv2ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 17 5","book":"1Sam","chapter":17,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָב֑וּשׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqsmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 17 38","book":"1Sam","chapter":17,"verse":38,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּלְבֵּ֨שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 17 38","book":"1Sam","chapter":17,"verse":38,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּלְבֵּ֥שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 28 8","book":"1Sam","chapter":28,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּלְבַּשׁ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"2Chr 5 12","book":"2Chr","chapter":5,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְלֻבָּשִׁ֣ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVPsmpa"},{"reference":"2Chr 6 41","book":"2Chr","chapter":6,"verse":41,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יִלְבְּשׁ֣וּ","source":"hebrew","mor